From: mecab <mecab@misosi.ru>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: pin 4addr unicast to the WDS peer

An AP vdev leaves unicast TX to the hardware address search: TCL looks up
the AST entry for the destination MAC (ADDRX) and transmits to whichever
peer owns it.  Commit 729cad3c3c9e ("wifi: ath12k: Add 4-address mode
support for eth offload") overrides that lookup with the 4addr peer's own
AST index, but only for multicast, which was the case it set out to fix.
Unicast relies on the WDS AST entries that firmware learns for clients
behind the peer.

That breaks when a client roams from this AP to a WDS repeater without
leaving.  Its direct peer stays on the pdev until hostapd removes it, and
meanwhile the search keeps resolving the client's address to that peer.
Frames that mac80211 hands down for the WDS peer (control->sta is the
4addr peer, the Ethernet DA is the roamed client) are sent to the absent
client, so DHCP and ARP replies never reach the repeater.  A stale peer
on another radio does no harm because the search is per pdev.

This patch pins unicast Ethernet frames for a 4addr peer on an AP vdev
to the peer's AST entry as well, so they go where mac80211 sent them.
The vendor driver does the same for any frame flagged as WDS extended:
its TX enqueue sets the index lookup override to the peer's AST entry
whether the destination is unicast or multicast [1][2].

The change is limited to AP vdevs.  STA vdevs already send to the AP
peer by index and are left as they were, as are frames to ordinary
clients.

[1] https://github.com/CodeLinaro-mirror/la_platform_vendor_qcom-opensource_wlan_qca-wifi-host-cmn-win/blob/57305a2d14c6c550206593edf29eb0d4804f608c/dp/wifi3.0/be/dp_be_tx.c#L1495-L1517
[2] https://github.com/CodeLinaro-mirror/la_platform_vendor_qcom-opensource_wlan_qca-wifi-host-cmn-win/blob/57305a2d14c6c550206593edf29eb0d4804f608c/dp/wifi3.0/dp_tx.c#L1214-L1221

Signed-off-by: mecab <mecab@misosi.ru>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
@@ -177,7 +177,16 @@
 	ti.bss_ast_hash = dp_link_vif->ast_hash;
 	ti.bss_ast_idx = dp_link_vif->ast_idx;
 
-	if (eth && is_multicast_ether_addr(eth->h_dest) && arsta) {
+	/* arsta is only set for 4-address (WDS) peers. On an AP, also pin
+	 * unicast for such a peer to its AST entry rather than letting the
+	 * hardware search by destination address: a client behind the WDS
+	 * peer may still have a stale direct peer on this pdev after roaming
+	 * away, and the DA search would deliver the frame to that absent
+	 * station instead.
+	 */
+	if (eth && arsta &&
+	    (ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_AP ||
+	     is_multicast_ether_addr(eth->h_dest))) {
 		ti.meta_data_flags = arsta->tcl_metadata;
 		ti.bss_ast_hash = arsta->ast_hash & ATH12K_AST_HASH_MASK;
 		ti.bss_ast_idx = arsta->ast_idx;
